               "headline":  "Record IPO fades: ANT slides 8.5% on day two, holding above $83",
               "summary":  "Anthropic listed on Nasdaq on 19 Nov 2026 after pricing a record $81.3B IPO at $83. Shares opened at $111.50 and closed day one at $97.17. On 20 Nov they fell 8.5% to $88.91 as an Nvidia-led AI selloff hit the market, and the intraday low of $83.05 nearly touched the offer price. The S-1 shows Q3 revenue of about $17B (up ~12x) and an ~$81B run-rate. It also shows a $1.26B nine-month operating loss and lock-ups that release shares in stages. Two days of trading are not enough to show a trend.",
