               "summary":  "Eaton (ETN) fell 5.82% on November 20, 2026, to $311.33—near its $308.22 52-week low and 34.9% below its $478 peak—despite reporting record Q3 results on November 3. Quarterly sales rose 28% year-over-year to $8.9 billion, data center revenue jumped 65%, electrical backlog exceeded $20 billion, and management raised full-year adjusted EPS guidance to $13.70–$13.80. Yet sector-wide AI capex fears and scrutiny of $20.1 billion in acquisition-driven debt triggered an Erste Group downgrade on November 18 and heavy technical selling. Technicals are bearish, while Eaton\u0027s long-term electrical moat remains intact.",
