               "summary":  "Alphabet (GOOGL) closed at $265.29 on November 20, 2026, barely above its $264.22 52-week low and 35% off its $408.61 peak. The slide accelerated after October 28 Q3 2026 results showed $51.4 billion in quarterly capex—driving -$9.1 billion free cash flow—and Search growth slowing from 17% to 12% on lower AI Mode monetization. Those pressures overshadowed Google Cloud\u0027s 103% jump to $30.7 billion and Anthropic\u0027s $121.3 billion Cloud commitment disclosed November 19. Technicals remain bearish despite oversold signals, keeping the long-term moat on watch.",
