               "caution":  "The sell-off from October\u0027s highs reflects real fundamental uncertainty, not just noise. Investors are repricing a balance sheet absorbing roughly EUR 6.0 billion in euro bonds (November 2) and US$10 billion in 5.7%-coupon dollar bonds (November 18) alongside EUR 6.0 billion in equity dilution to buy PTC at a 42.3% premium. S\u0026P expects FFO-to-debt to dip to 28%–30% in 2027. With shares hovering at EUR 226.55—just above EUR 223.45 support—any stumble in data-center orders or PTC regulatory clearance could test fresh 52-week lows.",
